// Expected: c1u0.
//
// Two shares of a 2-of-3 sharing travel in the clear, so the secret is
// recomposed and its confidentiality fails. The shares are still not linked:
// the only value the attacker holds that relates them is the secret it
// assembled out of the two of them, and in the world where share_b belongs
// to another sharing the same assembly yields some other value the attacker
// has nothing to compare against. Two points always lie on some line.
//
// The shared-secret witness used to accept that secret as a common origin,
// since withholding one share still left the recomposed secret in attacker
// knowledge and the split reconstructs each share from it. A value assembled
// from both queried values is no longer offered as their origin.
// unlink_shamir_origin.vp is the counterweight, where the secret is leaked
// independently of the shares and the link is genuine.

attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	generates secret
	share_a, share_b, share_c = THRESHOLD_SPLIT[2](secret)
]

Alice -> Bob: share_a, share_b

principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(share_a, share_b)
]

queries[
	confidentiality? secret
	unlinkability? share_a, share_b
]
